      "content": "Don't worry, literature questions about plot and character motivations can sometimes feel overwhelming when you look at the extract. \n\nIn *Cry, the Beloved Country*, Stephen Kumalo travels to Johannesburg to find his family members who left and never returned. When he arrives in Johannesburg, one of his first stops is to visit his brother, John Kumalo, who is now a successful politician living in the city.\n\nKeeping this context in mind, what is the main reason Stephen goes to see his brother John in this extract?"
