      "reasoning": "The learner understands the basic idea of irony but has not identified the two contrasting details. Use a familiar South African school situation to make the contrast visible, then ask one focused question without giving away the passage’s answer.",
      "content": "You have the idea that irony involves a contrast. Think of a school market day: a learner complains that the event crew does all the work so others can enjoy the day, but that learner also sits comfortably and enjoys it. In that example, what two things are being contrasted?"
